{"learnerLanguage":"pt","spokenSeconds":120,"turns":[{"speaker":"character","text":"So, shall we start with eating well? I think it's the most important one."},{"speaker":"learner","text":"Sorry if my accent is very Brazilian. Well, I partly agree. Eating well is essential, but I'd say doing exercise is more easy to fit into a busy day. What do you think about sleep?"},{"speaker":"character","text":"Good point. I reckon sleep is underrated, actually. Lots of students don't get enough."},{"speaker":"learner","text":"Exactly, that's true for me too. When I don't sleep well, I can't concentrate at all. On the other hand, it depends of your routine, some people simply work at night."},{"speaker":"character","text":"And what about spending time outdoors?"},{"speaker":"learner","text":"I think it's nice, but not everyone lives near a park. So maybe it's less important than the others. Shall we decide? I'd go for sleep, because without it nothing else works."},{"speaker":"character","text":"Yes, I think you've convinced me. Sleep it is."}],"criteria":[{"display":"band","halfBands":true,"levelBand":3,"maxBand":5,"scope":"test","key":"grammarVocabulary","name":"Grammar and Vocabulary","sound":false,"voiceOnly":false},{"display":"band","halfBands":true,"levelBand":3,"maxBand":5,"scope":"test","key":"discourse","name":"Discourse Management","sound":false,"voiceOnly":false},{"display":"band","halfBands":true,"levelBand":3,"maxBand":5,"scope":"test","key":"pronunciation","name":"Pronunciation","sound":true,"voiceOnly":true},{"display":"band","halfBands":true,"levelBand":3,"maxBand":5,"scope":"test","interactive":true,"key":"interaction","name":"Interactive Communication","sound":false,"voiceOnly":false},{"display":"band","halfBands":true,"levelBand":3,"maxBand":5,"scope":"test","key":"global","name":"Global Achievement","sound":false,"voiceOnly":false}],"exam":"cambridge","level":"B2","task":{"brief":"A discussion question with five written prompts around it (such as \"Is it easy to eat healthily these days?\"): two minutes of discussion, then a minute to decide on a second question. The two candidates may discuss the prompts in any order and needn't cover all of them; they aren't marked on reaching a decision.","minutes":{"max":4,"min":3},"name":"Part 3: Collaborative task","role":"partner"},"title":"B2 First"}